  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-05-18T00:37:54.291Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A lite edition that is the same as what's used for Quest/Android, but for PC.\n\nUse cases for this: \n\n(general) lower hardware floor for any headsets\n\n(better) prioritizes the same standards to lower CPU usage. Useful for those that want to use VRChat as VR work environments / streaming\n\nOverall, I think this would be an ideal scenario to have because regardless of the worlds I'm in, VRChat typically will take up the remaining CPU. I'd imagine utilizing a lightweight version will allow more resources to free up so that working on desktop could be more feasible.\n\ne.g. Using VRChat as a coworking space to do desktop work with friends without worrying about the game overly taking up resources and slowing down productivity elsewhere.",
